	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Duskwood is a forest of endless night in the south of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. Its old trees close overhead so that no true day ever reaches the ground. The dead walk its cemeteries, wolf-men prowl its groves and spiders nest along its rivers. In the east stands the town of {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link}, where the last folk who have not fled keep their torches lit and their doors barred.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[The forest was not always like this. Those who knew it before the wars remember green woods, busy farms and a village that has since taken the name {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link}. In the {link:first-war}First War{/link}, the {link:horde}Horde{/link} burned these woods as it burned {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link}. The farms were raised again afterward. Then, in the years when the men of the kingdom marched north to the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, something fouler came. A magic that no one in Darkshire can name seeped into the land. The leaves darkened, the graves opened, and the forest has lived in dusk ever since.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Duskwood stands alone. When the darkness came, {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} called its guards home and did not send them back. The town raised its own militia, the {link:the-night-watch}Night Watch{/link}, under {link:commander-althea-ebonlocke}Commander Althea Ebonlocke{/link}, and it has held the forest's heart with too few swords ever since. The Watch is not the only danger to {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link}'s peace. The lords of Stormwind overrule the sentences of its council, and one of its councilmen speaks openly of breaking with the crown. Beyond the walls, the {link:nightbane-worgen}Nightbane worgen{/link} have taken the south, the dead hold {link:raven-hill}Raven Hill{/link}, ogres hold the southern mounds, and the {link:defias-brotherhood}Defias Brotherhood{/link} use the western farms as a road for their schemes. Dark riders come out of {link:deadwind-pass}Deadwind Pass{/link} to the east, and no one knows what they want.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The folk of {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link}.{/b} Merchants, smiths, a seer, a historian and a council that still meets in the town hall. Most have lost someone to the forest.
• {b}{link:the-night-watch}The Night Watch{/link}.{/b} Watchers keep the town gates, the square and a handful of lonely posts on the roads.
• {b}The Carevin family.{/b} A household of hunters who wage their own war on demons and the undead.
• {b}The dead.{/b} Skeletons, ghouls and restless spirits fill {link:raven-hill-cemetery}Raven Hill Cemetery{/link} and the {link:tranquil-gardens-cemetery}Tranquil Gardens{/link}.
• {b}The {link:nightbane-worgen}Nightbane{/link}.{/b} Worgen who appeared as if out of the air, and who now hold the south of the forest.
• {b}The ogres.{/b} The Splinter Fist clan keeps the {link:vul-gol-ogre-mound}Vul'Gol Ogre Mound{/link}.
• {b}The Forsaken.{/b} A small expedition of the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} hides at {link:beggar-s-haunt}Beggar's Haunt{/link} in the far east.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Old Forest.{/b} Before the wars, the forest was green and its farms and villages prospered.
• {b}The {link:first-war}First War{/link}.{/b} The {link:horde}Horde{/link} burned the woods on its way to {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}.
• {b}The Darkening.{/b} In the years of the {link:third-war}Third War{/link}, a foul magic took hold of the forest. {link:raven-hill}Raven Hill{/link} fell and its people with it. Stormwind withdrew its guards, and {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link} raised the {link:the-night-watch}Night Watch{/link} in their place.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Darkshire holds, but barely, and its people have begun to wonder whether the kingdom still counts them among its own.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Wood",
			text = [=[• The children of {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link} are raised on a story of a kindly alchemist called the {link:abercrombie}Embalmer{/link}, who went mad with grief for his dead wife.
• The name of {link:stalvan-mistmantle}Stalvan Mistmantle{/link} is spoken in the town only in a whisper.
• Those who lose their way in the dark woods sometimes say a shadow led them back to the road.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Unrecorded",
			text = [=[No chronicle of these days records what first darkened Duskwood, or the year in which it happened.]=],
		},
