			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Morgan Ladimore was a knight who fought for the innocent and the poor. He married a girl named Lys when he was eighteen, and they had a son and two daughters. When war came to {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, he went north to fight at the side of {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther the Lightbringer{/link}. He came home to find his forest rotten and his house in ruins. Now he walks the cemetery as Mor'Ladim, a dead thing that kills without reason.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[{link:morgan-stern}Morgan{/link}'s fall is the saddest tale of {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link}. He was a good man broken by grief. His name is a warning of what the darkness of the forest can do even to the strongest heart.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
			text = [=[• He served {link:uther-the-lightbringer}Uther{/link} through the war in the north and saw the order of paladins disbanded, Uther slain and the plague spread.
